  "body": "Stacked on #961 (branch issue/869-coolant-air). Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed\n- New MCP tool `set_operation_coolant { name, coolant: off|flood|mist|air|through-tool }` (`crates/app/src/mcp/coolant_tools.rs`, row in the tools table). It runs the existing undoable `EditOperationParams::with_coolant` - one undo step, same door as the op page's picker. `through_tool`, spaces and any case are accepted on input.\n- Unknown mode or operation is refused by name (mode refusal lists the valid words).\n- A mode the op's machine has no coded entry for is still set, with a `warning` in the reply; the post does the refusing. Off and machines stating no coded coolant never warn.\n- `get_job` operations now carry `coolant`, so a headless agent can read it back.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/954-mcp-op-coolant.md`.\n\n## How tested\nPinned by `crates/app/tests/mcp_coolant.rs`: `the_tool_is_listed_with_its_mode_enum`, `air_sets_in_one_undo_step_and_redo_restores_it`, `unknown_modes_and_operations_are_refused_by_name`, `a_machine_without_the_mode_warns_and_one_with_it_does_not`, `the_coolant_round_trips_through_a_saved_project`. Quick gate (`--base origin/issue/869-coolant-air`) green: app lib plus 19 mcp-mapped suites; clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-app clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo script verb (MCP only). The camcraft-mcp skill's tool table is a process file and is not edited here; it needs the row `set_operation_coolant` (and `coolant` in get_job operations) in a process PR with a PROCESS_VERSION bump. No end-to-end post with a refused mode through MCP.\n\nChangelog: MCP `set_operation_coolant` sets an operation's coolant (off, flood, mist, air, through-tool) as one undo step; `get_job` shows it\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #954\n",
